{
  "cases": [
    {
      "id": "write_conditional_refuses_a_stale_write",
      "seq": 310070,
      "targets": [
        "s3",
        "s3-prefix"
      ],
      "read": "bounded",
      "ttl": 600,
      "write": "conditional",
      "scenario": [
        {
          "mutate": {
            "path": "/data/wp1.txt",
            "content": "v1\n"
          }
        },
        {
          "command": "cat /data/wp1.txt"
        },
        {
          "mutate": {
            "command": "cat /data/wp1.txt > /dev/null; echo B > /data/wp1.txt"
          }
        },
        {
          "command": "echo A > /data/wp1.txt; echo $?"
        },
        {
          "command": "cat /data/wp1.txt"
        }
      ],
      "note": "The shadow is a second mirage writer under the same policy: it reads, then writes B. The read side's If-Match carries the version its cat saw, the store refuses it (moto enforces PUT If-Match; both hosts run on it in CI), and the refused write drops the cached copy so the next cat prints B.",
      "expect": {
        "exit": 0,
        "stdout": "v1\n1\nB\n",
        "stderr": "/data/wp1.txt: changed since it was read; read it again before writing\n"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "write_conditional_keeps_a_current_write",
      "seq": 310071,
      "targets": [
        "s3",
        "s3-prefix"
      ],
      "read": "bounded",
      "ttl": 600,
      "write": "conditional",
      "scenario": [
        {
          "mutate": {
            "path": "/data/wp2.txt",
            "content": "v1\n"
          }
        },
        {
          "command": "cat /data/wp2.txt"
        },
        {
          "command": "echo x > /data/wp2.txt; echo $?"
        },
        {
          "command": "cat /data/wp2.txt"
        }
      ],
      "note": "The version the cat saw is still current, so the write goes through.",
      "expect": {
        "exit": 0,
        "stdout": "v1\n0\nx\n",
        "stderr": ""
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "write_conditional_without_a_version",
      "seq": 310072,
      "targets": [
        "s3",
        "s3-prefix"
      ],
      "read": "bounded",
      "ttl": 600,
      "write": "conditional",
      "scenario": [
        {
          "command": "echo x > /data/wp3new.txt; echo $?"
        },
        {
          "mutate": {
            "path": "/data/wp3.txt",
            "content": "v1\n"
          }
        },
        {
          "command": "echo y > /data/wp3.txt; echo $?"
        },
        {
          "command": "cat /data/wp3new.txt /data/wp3.txt"
        }
      ],
      "note": "With no version a write is a create (If-None-Match: *): a new name is written, a name the shadow already wrote is refused.",
      "expect": {
        "exit": 0,
        "stdout": "0\n1\nx\nv1\n",
        "stderr": "/data/wp3.txt: changed since it was read; read it again before writing\n"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "write_conditional_redirect_rewrite",
      "seq": 310073,
      "targets": [
        "s3",
        "s3-prefix"
      ],
      "read": "bounded",
      "ttl": 600,
      "write": "conditional",
      "scenario": [
        {
          "command": "echo a > /data/wp4.txt; echo b > /data/wp4.txt; cat /data/wp4.txt"
        }
      ],
      "note": "The first redirect keeps its bytes and the version its PUT returned, so the second redirect on the same line writes against it.",
      "expect": {
        "exit": 0,
        "stdout": "b\n",
        "stderr": ""
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "write_conditional_minio_refuses_copy_and_delete",
      "seq": 310074,
      "targets": [
        "object-storage-prefix"
      ],
      "read": "bounded",
      "ttl": 600,
      "write": "conditional",
      "scenario": [
        {
          "mutate": {
            "path": "/minio/wp5.txt",
            "content": "v1\n"
          }
        },
        {
          "command": "cat /minio/wp5.txt; cp /minio/wp5.txt /minio/wp5b.txt; echo $?"
        },
        {
          "command": "rm /minio/wp5.txt; echo $?"
        },
        {
          "command": "cat /minio/wp5.txt; ls /minio"
        }
      ],
      "note": "MinIO ignores copy and delete conditions (measured 2026-10-06), so the minio row has none and mirage refuses the copy and the delete itself, before any request; both leave the file as it was.",
      "expect": {
        "exit": 0,
        "stdout": "v1\n1\n1\nv1\nwp5.txt\n",
        "stderr": "cp: cannot create regular file '/minio/wp5b.txt': Operation not supported\nrm: cannot remove '/minio/wp5.txt': Operation not supported\n"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "write_unconditional_redirect_writes",
      "seq": 310075,
      "targets": [
        "s3",
        "s3-prefix"
      ],
      "read": "bounded",
      "ttl": 600,
      "write": "unconditional",
      "scenario": [
        {
          "mutate": {
